H1 = r"""Sixth pass: 2026-11-16 from 02:30 UTC (HEAD 536b7773 at its first run; the container had restarted at about 02:20, `uptime` said up 10 minutes at 02:30:56; the owner's full pause of 01:53 had been lifted at 02:32 by the orders recorded as DEC-OWNER-2026-11-16). What changed since the fifth pass is mostly one thing: **gate runners now exist**. `tools/bt/gates/` (34 tracked files) and `tests/governance/gates/` (36) hold executable runners for 11 of the 28 gates (Q01 to Q06, Q14, Q19, Q20, Q23 and Q25) with 585 unit tests, a mutation check of three of them (48 of 48 injected defects caught) and seven stored result files in this folder (`Q01.json`, `Q02.json`, `Q14.json`, `Q19.json`, `Q20.json`, `Q23.json`, `Q25.json`), every one with the verdict FAIL, for reasons that, as far as the failing items say, are the product's and the data's and not the runner's (the code of the runners was not audited here: 8.11). Section 2.6 describes the runners, their tests and what does not exist; section 3.0 is the one-page table of runner state per gate; every gate section of section 4 has an `Updated at pass 6` bullet; 3.1 lists what else moved. Statements of the earlier passes that say no gate runner exists (2.1) are true of the time they name and are superseded. New in the surroundings: the owner's orders of 16 November (no budget cap, so Q27 becomes a report; the 47 conflicts to be resolved by research, so the conflict inputs of Q02, Q04 to Q06, Q19, Q22 and Q28 will move; the owner's PC attached through Remote Control, which the session lists as a computer whose folder cannot be attached, so Q15 and the real-GPU parts of Q10 and Q24 stay NOT RUNNABLE HERE), and seven findings about the runners themselves (2.6 and 8.9: among them the `-I` import failure of two runners and the one-entry difference in counting unmarked register entries). What was run is in 7.8 and what was checked and corrected in 8.9 to 8.11. Nothing else of this file's contract changed: it describes what exists, defines no pass rule, sets no `passes` flag and lowers nothing."""

