S1 = r"""- At the sixth pass (16 November, 02:30 to about 03:30 UTC; outputs in `spec-b-evidence/pass6/`): `uptime` said up 10 minutes at 02:30:56, so the container had restarted at about 02:20 (the campaign log records the owner's full pause from 01:53 and the resumption at full throttle at 02:32). python 3.13.18, node v22.23.4 and Chrome for Testing 153.0.8010.12 are unchanged; numpy 2.5.3, Pillow 12.3.0, shapely 2.2.0, pyproj 3.8.0, OpenCV 5.0.0 and pandas 3.0.5 are present and scipy, astropy, skyfield, ephem, matplotlib, PyMuPDF, pytesseract and pytest are absent from the system python (the gate tests are python `unittest`); the scratch astropy environment `tmp/bt-gates/venv-astropy` is still there (85 MB). 15 GB RAM, 4 vCPUs; 6.9 GB free on the repository's volume at 02:57 (83 % used; 8.8 GB at 02:30: the scratch of every workstream counts, and this pass kept its scratch under `tmp/bt-gates/pass6`); load average 22 to 31 from 02:40 on, with 29 to 34 `tools/horde/bench.sh` processes waiting for the two slots of the machine lock and two `--timing` jobs of another workstream waiting for the lock alone (files `tmp/horde-timing.wanted.*`), which holds every newcomer back until all earlier holders have finished. Two locked jobs of this pass were queued behind them, job A at 02:36:20 and job C at 02:46:04 (their steps are in 7.8): {{LOCKSTATE}} The owner's PC: `list_computer_folders` (read-only, about 02:40 UTC) returned no usable folder: one entry, the computer MSI with the folder Claude, under `cannot_be_used` with the reason `not_available` (`pass6/list_computer_folders.out`); the campaign log (`horde/CAMPAIGN.md`, 02:44 UTC) records that the computer is connected through Remote Control, that its folder cannot be attached as a working folder from a cloud session and that the route that works is a session that runs on the PC (a read-only probe session started at 02:43 UTC after the owner's in-person approval). So the browser here is still software rendering only, and no frame time or picture of a real GPU can be measured by this container."""

S11 = r"""The specs' owner's work at the sixth pass (read at 02:3x to 02:5x UTC on 16 November and not reproduced; every statement is that owner's record): `app/tests/lib.mjs` gained the field `SLOW.stepMs` (the most the page's clock advances in one frame, 100 ms) so that a loop inside the page that must cover a span of the page's clock accumulates `min(frame time, SLOW.stepMs)` per frame, as `wait()` does; `scrub.spec.mjs` (its pop test) and `casualties.spec.mjs` (its return visit) were edited at 00:50 UTC for the reasons given under Q12, with the owner's verdicts HARNESS and STALE_TEST ("fixed; browser re-run pending"); `runs.tsv` has one new row (`diag-2-casualties-return`, 00:32:02 to 01:12:14 UTC, 2,412 s, exit 1) and `SW-STATUS.md` (committed 01:21) says "69 tests in 10 specs: 1 HARNESS, 1 NEEDS_GPU, 50 NOT, 15 PASS, 2 STALE_TEST" (at the fifth pass: 1 NEEDS_GPU, 51 NOT, 15 PASS, 1 STALE_TEST, 1 UNCLASSIFIED); four new node reproductions of browser tests (`sw-round-1/pre/arrival-window-node.mjs`, `fx-camera-at-spawn.mjs`, `scrub-node.mjs` and `structures-node.mjs`, each with its log) run the logic of a spec on the real layer without a browser in 2 to 11 s; and `sw-round-1/audit/assertion-audit-44857c38.log` (02:36 UTC) compares every `assert.*` call and every `t.gpuOnly` wrapper of the ten specs at commit 44857c38 with the working tree as multisets, so that a weakened assertion would show (it lists, for example, the 7 assertions removed from and the 13 added to `arrival.spec.mjs` with the delegated conflict defaults, and the 18 added to `leak.spec.mjs`). No spec has a new browser result and none can be met by software rendering where it names a frame time or a hardware picture."""

